{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed. The whole bug was one key name in `gen.py:13`.\n\n**The change:** `hr_target()` now emits `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}` instead of `\"value\": lo`. Per the colleague's note, `value`/`end` is routed by Intervals' FIT export as a zone-mapped (Lap-HR) target, so the watch clamps it to its own auto-detected bands — exactly what your notes document (every corridor landed on a watch zone edge: Z2, Z4, Z3, Z2). `start`/`end` routes as an instant-HR corridor, so the watch displays the raw bpm Intervals computes from its stored LTHR 172: warm-up 117–129, tempo 151–160, float 129–141, cool-down 112–124. The float corridor cross-checks nicely — it's the identical 75–82% range the colleague verified end-to-end.\n\n**Verification:** regenerated the event and diffed against `readback/event-184233-as-sent.json` — the only differences are the four `value` → `start` renames; units, bounds, durations, and the repeat block are untouched. I didn't push anything, per the ground rules, so the end-to-end watch check happens on your next push/sync.\n\n**From the colleague's note:** applied the `start`-vs-`value` key distinction (the fix), the point that \"%lthr is fine, absolute bpm isn't\" (so keeping percentage units was right), and the failed-attempts history, which matches your notes exactly. Didn't apply the `description`/text-grammar part — that fixes steps missing from the Intervals *web UI*, a symptom you don't have; your readback shows `workout_doc.steps` populated. Full write-up is in `ANSWER.md`."}
